  "verbalization": "Cephalexin, a cephalosporin antibiotic, is linked to Slc15a1 through a series of molecular relationships that ultimately converge on the gene responsible for transporting ions across cell membranes. The evidence suggests that Cephalexin, as part of the broader cephalosporin class, is included in the Cephalosporin category, which in turn includes Ceftizoxime and Ceftibuten. These antibiotics all bind to Slc15a1, a gene involved in ion transport, indicating a shared mechanism of action. The lowest common ancestors of these entities point to the broader class of cephalosporins, reinforcing the idea that the relationship between Cephalexin and Slc15a1 is rooted in their structural and functional similarities. The evidence supports a direct or indirect interaction through the cephalosporin class, highlighting a recurring mechanism of binding to Slc15a1. This connection is further supported by the presence of multiple pathways that converge on the same target gene, suggesting a consistent and significant biological role for Slc15a1 in the context of these antibiotics.",
